  "title": "IEEE1722: Don't reuse can.reserved in ACF CAN",
  "description": "ACF CAN reserves 3 high bits from a 32 bit word that stores a\n29 bit CAN identifier. Don't name these bits (a FT_UINT32) with\nthe \"can.reserved\" abbreviation, because that's already used by\nSocketCAN for a FT_BYTES, which is not a compatible field type.\n(SocketCAN uses those three bits for the eff, rtr, and esi bits,\nwhich are placed in a different location in IEEE 1722 ACF CAN.\nSocketCAN has reserved bytes elsewhere.) Just use a unique name.\n\nThere is some logic in having fields that correspond to the same\nthing have common abbreviations, but that doesn't apply to the\nreserved bits and bytes which are different in the various encodings.",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2024-12-17T00:20:22.523Z",
